# Datasets stay out of git. Their documentation does not: provenance, licences
# and checksums must be versioned even though the bytes are not.
data/**
!data/README.md
!data/LICENCES.md
!data/MANIFEST.csv
!data/raw/
!data/raw/yjmob100k/
!data/raw/yjmob100k/SOURCE.md
!data/raw/geolife/
!data/raw/geolife/SOURCE.md
!data/raw/_QUARANTINE_humob2024_4cities/
!data/raw/_QUARANTINE_humob2024_4cities/DO_NOT_USE.md

# Build artefacts and environments
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Derived result artefacts are EXCLUDED FOR ETHICS REASONS, not only for size.
#
# Every results/*.npz and results/*.pkl holds PER-USER arrays over the 24,517
# released pseudonyms: whether each person was re-identified correctly (y), the
# attack's confidence about them (p_platt, p_soft), their measured drift
# (comp, dec_*), their rarity (a_pop, a_knn, a_maha) and their per-condition
# swap outcomes. Codebase/paper/ETHICS.md section 5 commits this project to
# publishing "no per-user output of any kind ... no per-user drift values".
# Publishing these files would break that commitment.
#
# results/precheck_agg_*.tsv are aggregates, but ~29,000 of their rows are
# ABSOLUTE CELL COORDINATES with visit counts -- the spatial density signature
# of a city the release deliberately does not name. A published preprint
# (arXiv:2506.05611) recovered that city's geographic frame from exactly such
# density signatures, so these files are withheld as well.
#
# The written record (results/*.md) and the console transcripts
# (results/*_output.txt) carry no per-user rows and no cell coordinates; both
# were checked before the first push. Each results/*.md states the commands
# that regenerate its artefacts from the raw data.
results/*.npz
results/*.pkl
results/*.tsv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prose records stay out of git (author's decision, 2026-11-02). The repository
# carries the SCRIPTS and the RESULTS as text; the detailed written analyses --
# the design contract, the pre-registrations, and one .md per premise or
# objective explaining what each run means -- are kept with the manuscript
# instead. Every number quoted in those documents comes from a results/*.txt
# transcript that IS tracked here, so nothing in git depends on them.
*.md
